suggestion: By construction, for_team(other_team_id) is invoked when other_team_id differs from the contextual team. That's the API's whole point. The cache guard ctx.team_id == team_id always fails in that case, so every call hits Team. If for_team() is invoked in a loop (admin tooling, scheduled cross-team aggregations), this becomes N+1 on Team.
